# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gmail Outreach Automation — example crontab (macOS / Linux)
# Paths are pre-filled for this machine: /home/omsinghan/email-automation
#
# Install with:   crontab -e      (then paste ONE of the lines below)
# View current:   crontab -l
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Option A (recommended): check every 10 minutes and send whatever is now due.
# Resilient — if the machine is asleep at 8:00, the drafts still go out at the
# next check. send-due is a no-op when nothing is due.
*/10 * * * * /home/omsinghan/email-automation/run.sh send-due --campaign-id "quant-risk-june-2026" >> /home/omsinghan/email-automation/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Option B: fire once daily at 08:00 local time.
# 0 8 * * * /home/omsinghan/email-automation/run.sh send-due --campaign-id "quant-risk-june-2026" >> /home/omsinghan/email-automation/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Notes:
# - run.sh resolves its own directory, so cron's bare environment is fine.
# - Output (and any errors) are appended to logs/cron.log; app logs still go to
#   logs/outreach.log.
# - cron uses the machine's local timezone, matching the tool's scheduling.
